cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use the No Goals proof service, please cite this software."
type: software
title: "No Goals proof service: a Rust service for Lean proof checking and mathematical experiments"
authors:
  - family-names: Deeb
    given-names: Zeyad
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0009-9462-0369"
version: 0.1.15
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23632006
license: MIT
url: "https://www.zeyaddeeb.com/experiments/proofs"
repository-code: "https://github.com/zeyaddeeb/zeyaddeeb/tree/main/proofs"
abstract: >-
  Rust and Axum backend for No Goals, an interactive Lean 4 proof playground.
  The service checks bounded sequences of tactics against real Lean proof
  states, reports hypotheses and goals, and manages a pool of Lean REPL
  processes. It also includes an optional mathematical-experiment agent,
  persistent experiment records, and numerical instruments. This citation
  describes the proof service; the browser interface lives elsewhere in the
  same repository. Numerical experiments are not formal proofs.
keywords:
  - Lean
  - formal verification
  - interactive theorem proving
  - Rust
  - mathematical software
